      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When heat soak becomes excessively intense, the friction coefficient of brake pads typically decreases, a phenomenon known as brake fade. This drop occurs because excessive heat can degrade the pad material, leading to changes in the coefficient of friction and potentially gas buildup. On long mountain descents, this inconsistent performance translates to reduced braking power and an unpredictable feel. Therefore, effective heat management is crucial to maintain a stable friction coefficient throughout the entire braking event.",
